{
  "id": "spring-boot-security-jwt",
  "title": "JWT access tokens",
  "summary": "Connect familiar JWTs to Spring's decoder, principal, authorities, and revocation limits.",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLA3GkZPtsafacdBLdd3p1DyRd5FGfr3Ue",
  "updatedOn": "2026-10-20",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Engineering Digest: Complete JWT Authentication and Authorisation in Spring Boot",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qvAoUVXgpZg&list=PLA3GkZPtsafacdBLdd3p1DyRd5FGfr3Ue"
    },
    {
      "title": "Spring Security 6: JWT resource server",
      "url": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-security/reference/6.5/servlet/oauth2/resource-server/jwt.html"
    },
    {
      "title": "Spring Security 6: CSRF protection",
      "url": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-security/reference/6.5/servlet/exploits/csrf.html"
    },
    {
      "title": "JWT specification",
      "url": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "jwt-meaning",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JWT authentication in Spring Security"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-0-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Security's resource-server support authenticates an incoming JWT access token."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-0-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It replaces the password check for that API request."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-0-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The password-login lessons used "
        ],
        [
          "UserDetails",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " as the principal."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-0-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JWT resource-server authentication uses a "
        ],
        [
          "Jwt",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " principal by default."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-0-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It does not call "
        ],
        [
          "UserDetailsService",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " to load a password account for each token."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "jwt-validation",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Token validation"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-1-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JwtDecoder",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " checks the signed token before Spring trusts its claims."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-1-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The decoder needs trusted issuer settings and trusted signing keys."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-1-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The application must require the audience intended for its API."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-1-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring's issuer-based configuration validates the signature, issuer, and applicable expiry and not-before timestamps."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-1-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Audience validation is an additional requirement configured in the resource-server lesson."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-1-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Decoding a payload in a browser does not perform Spring Security's server-side validation."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "jwt-claims",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Claims and Spring authentication"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JwtAuthenticationToken",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is the authenticated "
        ],
        [
          "Authentication",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " produced for a valid JWT."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Its principal is the validated "
        ],
        [
          "Jwt",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Authentication.getName()",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " uses the token's "
        ],
        [
          "sub",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " claim by default."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Token scopes become granted authorities through "
        ],
        [
          "JwtAuthenticationConverter",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A valid signature does not give the token permission to call every endpoint."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The request rules still check the resulting authorities."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-table-0",
      "type": "table",
      "columnOrder": [
        "0",
        "1"
      ],
      "hasColumnHeader": true,
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-table-0-row-0",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "Token field"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "Spring configuration or access"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-table-0-row-1",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "iss",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "The configured "
              ],
              [
                "issuer-uri",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              [
                " identifies the trusted issuer."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-table-0-row-2",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "aud",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "The configured "
              ],
              [
                "audiences",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              [
                " requires the intended API audience."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-table-0-row-3",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "sub",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "The default authenticated name comes from this subject."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-table-0-row-4",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "exp",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              [
                " and "
              ],
              [
                "nbf",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "Timestamp validators check token validity times."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "security-jwt-lesson-2-table-0-row-5",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "scope",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              [
                " or "
              ],
              [
                "scp",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "The default converter creates "
              ],
              [
                "SCOPE_",
                [
                  [
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              [
                " authorities."
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "jwt-bearer",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Principal access"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-3-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@AuthenticationPrincipal Jwt jwt",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " supplies the validated JWT to a controller parameter."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-3-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "jwt.getSubject()",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " reads its subject."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-3-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "jwt.getClaimAsString(\"email\")",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " reads an email claim if the issuer includes it."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-3-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A claim used for authorization needs a documented meaning from the trusted issuer."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-3-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The ownership check still needs the subject mapped to the correct local account."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "jwt-lifecycle",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Expiration and logout"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-4-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The resource server normally validates each JWT locally using trusted public keys."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-4-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It does not automatically ask the issuer whether the user logged out or a token was revoked."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-4-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Ending a browser session does not invalidate an already issued JWT access token."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-4-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Immediate revocation needs an additional design, such as a server-side revocation check or token introspection."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-4-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The next OAuth2 lesson places the issuer, client, and resource server in the same flow."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "security-jwt-lesson-4-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The resource-server lesson then configures the decoder and permissions."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
